All accepted strings are exactly the prefixes of the deterministic infinite word generated by the rules  
c → ca, ca → cab, cab → cabcab, … and  
b → ba | bc, ba → bab, bab → baba | babca, baba → babab | babaa, babca → babcab, …  
Thus a string is accepted iff it follows the unique continuation constraints:
- after “c” only “a” may follow;
- after “ca” only “b” may follow;
- after “cab” the only possible continuation is the block “c a b” repeated any number of times;
- after “b” either “a” or “c” may follow;
- after “ba” only “b” may follow;
- after “bab” either “a” or the block “c a” may follow;
- after “baba” the next symbol may be “a” or “b”, and the pattern then repeats analogously.  
